{'symbol': 'PEG', 'date': '2020-05-04 10:30:00', 'title': 'Pseg Announces 2020 First Quarter Results', 'text': 'PSEG ANNOUNCES 2020 FIRST QUARTER RESULTS.SEES FY 2020 NON-GAAP OPERATING EARNINGS PER SHARE $3.30 TO $3.50.PUBLIC SERVICE ENTERPRISE GROUP - QTRLY EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.88.PUBLIC SERVICE ENTERPRISE GROUP - QTRLY NON-GAAP OPERATING EARNINGS $1.03 PER SHARE.PUBLIC SERVICE ENTERPRISE GROUP - QTRLY  OPERATING REVENUES $2,781 MILLION VERSUS $2,980 MILLION.RE-AFFIRMS NON-GAAP 2020 OPERATING EARNINGS GUIDANCE OF $3.30 - $3.50 PER SHARE.PUBLIC SERVICE ENTERPRISE GROUP - PSE&G SERVICE TERRITORY EXPERIENCED DECLINE OF ABOUT 5% TO 7% IN ELECTRIC LOAD FROM END OF MARCH THROUGH APRIL.PUBLIC SERVICE ENTERPRISE GROUP - ANTICIPATE REDUCTION IN ELECTRIC LOAD FOR PSE&G SERVICE TERRITORY MAY EXTEND THROUGH Q2 AND POSSIBLY LONGER.PUBLIC SERVICE ENTERPRISE GROUP - REMAIN COMMITTED TO EXECUTING OUR FIVE-YEAR, $12 TO $16 BILLION CAPITAL PLAN WITHOUT NEED TO ISSUE EQUITY.PUBLIC SERVICE ENTERPRISE GROUP - IMPROVED OUR NET LIQUIDITY POSITION, ENDING MARCH WITH APPROXIMATELY $4 BILLION OF AVAILABLE LIQUIDITY.PUBLIC SERVICE ENTERPRISE GROUP - COVID-19 RELATED REDUCTION IN DEMAND APPEARED LATE IN QUARTER.'}
{'symbol': 'SRE', 'date': '2020-05-04 10:30:00', 'title': 'Sempra Energy Reports First-Quarter 2020 Earnings Results', 'text': 'REPORTS FIRST-QUARTER 2020 EARNINGS RESULTS.Q1 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $3.08.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.53.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $2.26 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.REAFFIRMS FY 2020 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $6.70 TO $7.50.REAFFIRMING ITS FULL-YEAR 2021 EPS GUIDANCE RANGE OF $7.50 TO $8.10..MAINTAINING STRONG LIQUIDITY POSITION.FY2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $7.14 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FY2021 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $7.88 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.UPDATED FULL-YEAR 2020 GAAP EPS GUIDANCE RANGE IS $11.88 TO $13.02.QTRLY TOTAL REVENUES $3,029 MILLION VERSUS $2,898 MILLION.REAFFIRMING ITS FULL-YEAR 2021 EPS GUIDANCE RANGE OF $7.50 TO $8.10.Q1 REVENUE VIEW $3.09 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FY RUN-RATE EARNINGS FROM PHASE 1 LIQUEFACTION-EXPORT PROJECT ANTICIPATED TO BE BETWEEN $400 MILLION & $450 MILLION ANNUALLY STARTING IN 2021.GIVEN CURRENT MARKET DYNAMICS, FINAL INVESTMENT DECISION NOW EXPECTED IN 2021 FOR PORT ARTHUR LNG LIQUEFACTION PROJECT.'}
