{'symbol': 'TSN', 'date': '2020-05-04 10:30:00', 'title': 'Tyson Foods Reports Q2 Sales of $10.89 Bln', 'text': 'TYSON FOODS REPORTS SECOND QUARTER 2020 RESULTS.Q2 SALES $10.89 BILLION.Q2 REVENUE ESTIMATE $10.96 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q2 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.77.Q2 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.00.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.04 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.HAVE INSTITUTED SAFEGUARDS THAT MEET OR EXCEED CDC AND OSHA GUIDELINES AT ALL FACILITIES.QTRLY SALES $10.89 BILLION VERSUS $10.44 BILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.REMAIN FOCUSED ON DRIVING LONG-TERM GROWTH.Q2 REVENUE VIEW $10.96 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.CANNOT ANTICIPATE HOW LONG CHALLENGES PRESENTED BY COVID-19 WILL PERSIST.EXPERIENCING MULTIPLE CHALLENGES RELATED TO COVID-19 PANDEMIC.EXPECT INDUSTRY FED CATTLE SUPPLIES TO INCREASE APPROXIMATELY 2% IN FISCAL 2020 AS COMPARED TO FISCAL 2019.EXPECT INDUSTRY HOG SUPPLIES TO INCREASE APPROXIMATELY 5% IN FISCAL 2020 AS COMPARED TO FISCAL 2019.TYSON FOODS - COVID-19 RELATED CHALLENGES ANTICIPATED TO INCREASE OPERATING COSTS AND NEGATIVELY IMPACT VOLUMES FOR REMAINDER OF FISCAL 2020.RECENT DATA INDICATES THAT CHICKEN PRODUCTION FOR REMAINDER OF FISCAL 2020 WILL BE LOWER THAN THOSE PROJECTIONS.OPERATIONALLY, HAVE AND EXPECT TO CONTINUE TO FACE SLOWDOWNS AND TEMPORARY IDLING OF PRODUCTION FACILITIES.FOR REMAINDER OF FISCAL 2020, DO NOT BELIEVE CHICKEN PRICING WILL IMPROVE.TYSON FOODS - LOWER LEVELS OF PRODUCTIVITY,HIGHER COSTS OF PRODUCTION CO EXPERIENCED TO LIKELY CONTINUE IN SHORT TERM UNTIL EFFECTS OF COVID-19 DIMINISH.'}
